    ],
    ans: 1,
    exp: "In parallel, all appliances get the full 220V supply voltage, total resistance decreases, and if one appliance fails, others continue working."
  },
  {
    q: "According to Joule's law of heating, the heat produced in a resistor of resistance R carrying current I for time t is given by:",
    opts: ["H = I·R·t", "H = I²·R·t", "H = I·R²·t", "H = I²·R²·t"],
    ans: 1,
    exp: "Joule's law states H = I²Rt. Heat is directly proportional to the square of current, resistance, and time."
  },
  {
    q: "An electric iron consumes 1 kW electric power when operated at 220 V. The current flowing through it is approximately:",
    opts: ["0.22 A", "4.55 A", "10 A", "2.2 A"],
    ans: 1,
    exp: "P = V · I ⟹ I = P / V = 1000 W / 220 V ≈ 4.545 A ≈ 4.55 A."
  },
  {
    q: "1 Kilowatt-hour (kWh), the commercial unit of electrical energy, is equal to:",
    opts: ["3.6 × 10⁵ J", "3.6 × 10⁶ J", "36 × 10⁶ J", "1000 J"],
